-- title:
--   Constant field extension at a place with separable residue field
-- statement:
--   Let $k$, $K$, $F_0$, $F$ be fields with $k$-algebra structures on $K$, $F_0$, $F$ and a $K$-algebra, resp. $F_0$-algebra, structure on $F$, compatible in the sense that $k \to K \to F$ and $k \to F_0 \to F$ are scalar towers. Assume: there is an $x \in F$ with $F$ finite-dimensional and separable over the intermediate field $K(x)$; the subfield of $F$ generated by $K$ together with the image of $F_0$ is all of $F$; and $K$ and the image of $F_0$ are linearly disjoint over $k$ in the elementwise form that for every finite family $f : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to F_0$ that is $k$-linearly independent and every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to K$ with $\sum_i c_i f_i = 0$ in $F$ one has $c_i = 0$ for all $i$. Let $v$ be a place of $F_0$ over $k$, i.e. a valuation subring $\mathcal{O}_v \subsetneq F_0$ containing $k$ and which is a principal ideal ring, and assume its residue field $\kappa(v)$ is finite-dimensional and separable over $k$. Then: (i) the set of places $W$ of $F$ over $K$ with $(\mathcal{O}_W)^{-1}$-pullback along $F_0 \to F$ equal to $\mathcal{O}_v$ is finite; (ii) every such $W$ satisfies $\mathrm{ord}_W(f) = \mathrm{ord}_v(f)$ for all $f \in F_0$, where $\mathrm{ord}$ is minus the logarithm of the associated $\mathbb{Z}^{m0}$-valued adic valuation, and $\kappa(W)$ is finite over $K$; (iii) for every finite set $T$ of places of $F$ over $K$ whose members are exactly the places lying over $v$ in this sense, $\sum_{W \in T} \dim_K \kappa(W) = \dim_k \kappa(v)$.
--
--   This is the classical description of the behaviour of a place of a function field under an arbitrary extension of the constant field, at a place whose residue field is separable over the small constant field: no ramification occurs and the residue degrees upstairs add up to the degree downstairs. It is used in the construction of evaluation maps on annuli in the node annulus machinery, via [`AlgebraicCurve.NodeAnnulusEngine.exists_mem_and_forall_evalAt_eq_coe_apply_of_ringHom_quotient`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.NodeAnnulusEngine.exists_mem_and_forall_evalAt_eq_coe_apply_of_ringHom_quotient).
